###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training cost in V100 GPU-hours (Tables 6 and 8) is on each run
# (gpuHours); inference throughput in structures per GPU second (Table 8) is
# on the validation result of the corresponding model as inferenceHardware.
# ML relaxations cost 1011 GPU-hours (IS2RE/IS2RS) and 1075 GPU-hours
# (AdsorbML) for the 153M model, 240 and 298 for the 31M model (App. D.3).

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - EquiformerV2 is built 'Starting from Equiformer' by replacing its SO(3) convolutions with eSCN convolutions and adding three architectural changes (Abstract, Sec. 3). Recorded in the registry as EquiformerV2 derived from Equiformer (new registry method, trained here in Table 6). eSCN is not a registry method; its contribution is not recorded as a derivation edge.
# - OC20 and OC22 energy errors are in meV per structure (adsorption energies for OC20, total energies for OC22). The OC22 linear reference is used for both models.
# - The S2EF-2M base model's errors are those of Table 1a index 5 (equal to Table 6, Lmax 6). Settings of the Lmax 2 and 4 models and of Equiformer other than Lmax are those of the base setting with reduced widths (App. D.2) and are not encoded. The 122M parameter count of the OC22 models is in their labels.
# - IS2RS AFbT/ADwT, IS2RE relaxed-energy MAEs, AdsorbML success rates and the eleven other QM9 targets are not encoded; the QM9 Noisy Nodes variant (Table 12) is not encoded.
# - The DFT level of OC20, OC22 and QM9 is not described in this paper; the data sets carry no reference calculation here. Sizes of the S2EF-All and All+MD splits are not stated (OC20 is 'about 130M structures').
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liao2023.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

